<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7042"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i found the following at: <BR><a href="http://www.angelfire.com/nc/crimeinformation/murder.htm" target=_top>http://www.angelfire.com/nc/crimeinformation/murde r.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Do you know anything about these cases? <BR>Im trying to learn more about these cases. They mysteriously dont have a location or much information at the website. Ive emailed the owner and haven&#39;t heard back...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
