<!--Post: 7134--><!--Time: 1108223823-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7134"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good read, here is one excerpt from this site: <BR> <BR>&#34;Bobby Joe Long  A distant cousin of Henry Lee Lucas, Bobby suffered from a hereditary disorder in which he had an extra &#34;X&#34; chromosome which made his glands produce abnormal amounts of estrogen. In other words, Bobby had breasts. Adding to his confusion his mother slept with him until he was thirteen.  <BR> <BR>After suffering a head injury from a motorcycle accident, Bobby Joe turned into a lust machine. He masturbated five times a day in addition to the two daily sessions with his wife. Not satisfied he began stalking for new dates. From 1980 to 1983 Bobby was busy raping fifty women in the Miami/Fort Lauderdale area. In 1984, after moving back to the Tampa Bay area, he graduated to murder. His victims of choice were prostitutes whom he considered scum. &#34; <BR> <BR>     A possible solution for our X Factor mystery, and the possible reason for masturbating so many times at the scenes. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7134-->
<!--Post: 7692--><!--Time: 1108657546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 8:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ok. i got a response regarding the following cases... <BR>1. In 1985, an unknown assailant raped and murdered a 32 year old female and killed two of her small children. All three were stabbed multiple times and their throats were cut. The mother&#39;s hands had been bound with some type of cord and a pillow had been placed over her face. There was no sign of forced entry. The victim had recently placed an ad in the local paper. Some correspondence was received from a &#34;Mr. X&#34; claiming responsibility.  <BR> <BR>2. In 1985 an unknown assailant raped and murdered a 32 year old female. She had been stabbed multiple times and her throat was cut. Her hands had been bound with some type of cord and a pillow had been placed over her face. There was no sign of forced entry. The victim had recently placed an ad in the local paper.   <BR> <BR>Response: <BR>Hi: <BR>    Thank you for your inquiry.  The postings are several years old and it might take some time to find the submissions. <BR>    I have some limited information as to where the crimes occurred.  The first one occurred in Fayetteville, North Carolina and the second one about fifty miles away in Bolivia, North Carolina. <BR>    There was a conviction in the first case but the defendant was acquitted in a second trial.  A book came out about the case.  It was &#34;Innocent Victims&#34; by Scott Whistnant.  The case was also published in a book entitled &#34;Witness for the Defense,&#34; by Dr. Elizabeth Loftus. <BR>  <BR>  No one was ever arrested in the second case.  They both happened around the same time frame. <BR>  <BR>I wish I had more information but if you have specific questions I can try to locate the submission. <BR>  <BR>THEN I ASKED IF THERE WAS A POSITIVE DNA MATCH... <BR>Response: <BR>No.  these crimes occurred in the mid-1980&#39;s an DNA wasn&#39;t available.  Now that it is, the State still considers the first one closed because someone was arrested.  The other one is probably sitting deep in a cold case file somewhere.  I don&#39;t know where you&#39;re from but in this State a criminal case is considered closed at the time a suspected is arrested.  If he is found not guilty, the case remains in the solved category.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7692-->
<!--Post: 7752--><!--Time: 1108672490-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7752"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nm_pi <BR> <BR>Number 5 on that site you listed is creepy, too.  A young mother and her two sons were the victims in this case. While none of BTK&#39;s known victims were left in a bathtub, the hands and feet of the vics were tied with telephone cord and they were strangled as well as drowned.   <BR> <BR>The murders happened during the day, their car was taken and left elsewhere, and there was no sign of robbery or sexual assault. <BR> <BR>This happened in Houston, TX in May 1978.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7752-->
